{
    "background_story": "Shelby was a truck driver with a no-nonsense attitude and a heart of gold. She spent years hauling goods across the country, earning a reputation as one of the most reliable and efficient drivers on the road. But after a decade of living out of a suitcase, Shelby felt the weight of her grueling schedule bearing down on her. She longed to unload the stress and responsibility that came with her job. So, she made the bold decision to leave the trucking industry behind and pursue her true passion: photography. Shelby traded in her rig for a camera and began capturing the beauty of the world around her. As she traveled, she finally felt free to unload the emotional baggage that had accumulated over the years, finding peace and creative expression behind the lens.",
